exports[`prompt del classificatore > should number the generated views after the two pictures and the difference last, with their rules 1`] = `
"Part to recognise: «Fibbia del cinturino» (name: Fibbia; material: ottone; colour: oro antico).
Vertical: footwear. Other parts in the picture: Cinturino, Tomaia.
Declared type: buckle (source: catalogo). The family is FIXED: \`fibbia\` — choose only variant, view, scale and parameters.
Known scale: 20 mm = inner_width_mm (source: catalogo (supplier catalogue), confidence 0.9); measured on the mask: 11.2 px/mm in the original picture (≈ 15.568 px/mm in picture 1).
The mask is a precise segmentation.
Picture 1: the part cropped (its box + 15 %), long side 1024 px, the mask outline drawn in red. Scale factor of the crop: 1.39 crop px per original px. Picture 2: the whole picture reduced to 512 px, the part's box highlighted.
Picture 3: the MAIN VIEW — a flat orthographic picture of the part alone, GENERATED from picture 1 by an image model, looking straight at the face \`fianco_esterno\`.
Picture 4: the CONTROL VIEW — a flat orthographic picture of the part alone, GENERATED from picture 1 by an image model, looking straight at the face \`dietro\`.
Read profiles and ratios from the main view, thicknesses and depths from the control view.
Picture 1 (the photo) decides what exists and the materials: where a generated view contradicts the photo, the photo wins and your confidence goes down.
\`vista.*\` always describes picture 1 (the photo), never a generated view.
Proportions measured on the photo, without perspective correction (reliability 0.8; the product is the union of 4 part boxes): part height / product length = 0.313; part height / product height = 0.7. Use them only where nothing better is readable, with \`fonte: "proporzione"\`; a low reliability means a perspective or a partial framing.
The part is whole in the photo.
Picture 5: the silhouette of the model built from your previous answer (red) over the mask (blue) does not match: is the family, the variant or the view wrong? Answer again from scratch.
Write \`motivo\`, \`domande.motivo\` and \`note\` in Italian."
`;
